  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Comprehensive Protection Services to Child Victims of TIP Crimes and Those At Risk of Being Trafficked in Nicaragua</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Casa Alianza Nicaraguas (CANs) FY2012 proposal builds on the many accomplishments of their 2008-2010 and 2011-2012 J/TIP projects, and presents innovative strategies to expand Nicaraguas efforts to raise awareness, protect children who have been trafficked and are at risk of being trafficked, and institutionalize systems designed to more effectively prosecute traffickers. Under &quot;Prevention&quot; they will amplify the reach and content of their already extensive &quot;NO a La Trata&quot; campaign. Under &quot;Protection &quot; CAN will continue to provide street outreach and a multidisciplinary residential treatment program for 600 child victims and potential child victims of trafficking in a country where these kinds of services are simply not available They will also undertake a study geared to measure the impact of our protection and treatment services.</narrative>
  </description>
